X:1
T:Splinter Mcleod's Jig
% NFF Book 2023
S:collected from Norm McConnell, Echlin South, Vic, fiddler
S:collected by John Meredith, NLA Bib ID 2066986
N:This is a version of the waltz "Viennese Nights" collected from Harry Cotter, Binalong, NSW
H:John Meredith records that McConnell learnt this tune from Scottish Piper
H:and drummer 'Splinter' McLeod, at Noorat sometime in the 1920s.  The original
H:is undiscovered as yet however, the tune appears in an audio visual as 
H:"La Valse Du Mariage",  Guidry Brothers 1929.
B:J Meredith, R Covell, & P Brown, Folk Songs of Australia Vol 2, UNSW Press, 1987, p311
R:Jig
F:Splinter_Mcleods_Jig.mp3 Splinter Mcleod's Jig - played by Ray Mulligan
